      "narrative": "Mara Venn sets down her copper mug, the metal clinking against the scarred wood. Her sharp eyes hold yours for a moment before she speaks, her voice low and even.\n\n\"The Ash Gate?\" She leans forward, charcoal coat rustling. \"It's been sealed for near a decade now. Locked by order of the Kestrel Guild after what came through from the other side.\" She pauses, fingers tracing the rim of her mug. \"Toran there \u2014\" she tilts her head toward the nervous clerk at the corner table, \"\u2014 he's the lockwright who maintained it for years. Sworn to the Guild's secrecy, but he knows its workings better than anyone alive.\"\n\nShe glances at the shuttered window, as if the gate might be visible through the wood.\n\n\"Old Bram was the ferryman. Used to carry people through, back when passage was legal. He's dead now \u2014 found at the gate's foot three winters past, frozen solid, keys still in his hand.\" Her jaw tightens. \"The Guild sealed it proper after that. No one's been through since.\"\n\nShe looks back at you, waiting for your next question."
    },
