      "narrative": "Mara's eyebrow lifts slightly as the question lands. She taps a finger on her mug, thinking.\n\n\"Before it was filed... that'd be Grom. Local blacksmith, worked out of a forge down near the old mill road. He handled all the heavy ironwork on the gate \u2014 the hinges, the crossbars, the lock housing itself. Toran did the fine mechanism work, but Grom was the one who shaped the metal around it.\"\n\nShe takes a slow drink, then adds, \"His work was solid. Never had a complaint about the gate's iron while he was alive. But then...\" She sets the mug down. \"He turned up dead a few weeks before Old Bram. Throat cut, found behind his own forge. The Guild called it a robbery gone wrong, but the timing always sat wrong with me.\"\n\nShe watches you, letting that sink in. \"Why the interest in Grom specifically?\""
    },
