      "narrative": "Mara's fingers still on the mug. Her eyes narrow, not with suspicion but with the careful precision of someone deciding exactly how much to say.\n\n\"The Guild appointed a toll-keeper,\" she says slowly. \"Name was Sable Quill. Travel-stained cloak, always coming or going. He kept the ledger, collected the fees, decided who crossed and who didn't.\"\n\nShe scrapes a thumbnail along a groove in the table. \"He's still around. I saw him at the gate just this morning, actually. Looked like he was waiting for something. Or someone.\"\n\nShe holds your gaze. \"You want my advice? If you're looking for answers about the gate, Sable's the one who held the keys \u2014 not just to the lock, but to the list of every soul who paid to pass through.\""
    },
