      "narrative": "The door of the Copper Finch swings shut behind you, cutting off the tavern's warmth. Morning air hits your face \u2014 damp, cold, carrying the smell of wet stone and distant woodsmoke.\n\nThe path to the Ash Gate is short. Fifty paces along a cobbled lane between shuttered storefronts, then a left turn onto a gravel track that winds through a stand of skeletal birch trees. Their white trunks peel in the damp.\n\nThen the trees part.\n\nThe Ash Gate stands alone in a clearing of packed earth and scattered dead leaves. A cracked black arch, fifteen feet tall, its surface pitted and scarred by weather. The arch frames nothing \u2014 just grey sky and the suggestion of a path beyond, though your eye slides off it, unable to focus on what lies past the threshold.\n\nA figure stands beside the gate. Travel-stained cloak, hood drawn up against the morning chill. He's not looking at you yet \u2014 he's staring at the arch's keystone, where the lock mechanism sits. A complex brass plate, its surface scoured clean of any markings, the keyhole filed down to a smooth, impassable blank."
    },
