      "narrative": "The name hangs in the cold air for a moment, swallowed by the silence of the clearing.\n\nNothing.\n\nThe birch trees don't stir. The grey sky holds still. The hooded figure at the gate doesn't turn.\n\nThen you notice it \u2014 a shift in the air. Not a sound, but its absence. The faint rustle of dead leaves that had been moving stops. The world holds its breath.\n\nThe hooded figure finally moves. He turns his head, just slightly, enough for you to catch the edge of a weathered jaw beneath the hood's shadow.\n\n\"You're calling for a dead man,\" he says. His voice is flat, unhurried. \"He's been frozen at this gate for three winters. You won't get an answer.\"\n\nHe turns back to the keystone, running a gloved finger along the filed-down keyhole.\n\n\"But maybe that's not who you're really asking about.\""
    },
